#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:1
msgid "CUDA and ROCm Stub Libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:3
msgid ""
"This document describes TileLang's stub mechanism for GPU driver/runtime "
"libraries (CUDA and ROCm/HIP)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:6
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:8
msgid "CUDA:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:10
msgid ""
"**CUDA Driver (`cuda_stub`)**: Allows TileLang to be imported on systems "
"without a GPU (e.g., CI/compilation nodes) by lazy-loading `libcuda.so` only "
"when needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:13
msgid ""
"**CUDA Runtime & Compiler (`cudart_stub`, `nvrtc_stub`)**: Resolves SONAME "
"versioning mismatches (e.g. `libcudart.so.11` vs `libcudart.so.12`), "
"enabling a single build to work across different CUDA versions. This is "
"achieved by reusing CUDA libraries already loaded by frameworks like PyTorch "
"when possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:19
msgid "ROCm:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:21
msgid ""
"**HIP Runtime/Module API (`hip_stub`)**: Allows TileLang to be imported on "
"systems without ROCm installed by lazy-loading `libamdhip64.so` only when "
"needed. The stub also prefers already-loaded symbols via `RTLD_DEFAULT` / "
"`RTLD_NEXT` to interoperate with frameworks that have already loaded HIP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:25
msgid ""
"**HIP Runtime Compiler (`hiprtc_stub`)**: Lazily loads `libhiprtc.so` and "
"exposes the minimal HIPRTC API subset used by TileLang/TVM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:28
msgid "Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:30
msgid "The stubs in `src/target/stubs/` implement a lazy-loading mechanism:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:32
msgid ""
"**Lazy Loading**: Libraries are loaded via `dlopen` only upon the first API "
"call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:33
msgid ""
"**Global Symbol Reuse**: For `cudart` and `nvrtc`, the stubs first check the "
"global namespace (`RTLD_DEFAULT`) to use any already loaded symbols (e.g., "
"from PyTorch)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:34
msgid ""
"**ROCm Notes**: `hip_stub` checks `RTLD_DEFAULT` / `RTLD_NEXT` first and "
"then falls back to `dlopen(\"libamdhip64.so\")`. It additionally provides "
"wrappers for `hsa_init` / `hsa_shut_down` so that ROCm-enabled wheels do not "
"record a hard dependency on `libhsa-runtime64` at import time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:38
msgid ""
"**Versioning Support**: Handles ABI differences between CUDA versions (e.g., "
"`cudaGraphInstantiate` changes in CUDA 12)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:40
msgid "Build Option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:42
msgid ""
"`TILELANG_USE_CUDA_STUBS` (Default: `ON`) controls CUDA stubs. When enabled, "
"TileLang links against these stubs instead of the system CUDA toolkit "
"libraries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../runtime_internals/stubs.md:45
msgid ""
"`TILELANG_USE_HIP_STUBS` (Default: `ON`) controls ROCm stubs. When enabled "
"(and `USE_ROCM=ON`), TileLang/TVM link against `hip_stub` / `hiprtc_stub` "
"instead of the system ROCm libraries."
msgstr ""
